      "parsed_output": {
        "files_changed": [
          "agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/util/IoUtil.java",
          "agent/core/src/main/java/org/jolokia/http/AgentServlet.java",
          "agent/jvm/src/main/java/org/jolokia/jvmagent/handler/JolokiaHttpHandler.java",
          "agent/core/src/test/java/org/jolokia/util/IoUtilTest.java"
        ],
        "patch_notes": "Root cause: the JSONP `callback` parameter reached the response as `callback + \\\"(\\\" + json + \\\");\\\"` served with Content-Type text/javascript, with no validation, in both the servlet agent (AgentServlet.sendResponse -> IoUtil.streamResponseAndClose / sendAllJSON) and the JVM agent (JolokiaHttpHandler.sendStreamingResponse / sendAllJSON). A crafted callback such as `<script>alert(1)</script>` was reflected unescaped.\n\nFix: Added `IoUtil.validateCallback(String)` which returns the callback only if it matches `^[A-Za-z_$][A-Za-z0-9_$.]*$` (a valid JS function reference), otherwise null. This blocks characters like `<`, `>`, `\"`, `'`, `(`, `;` and whitespace used for injection. Applied the helper:\n- AgentServlet.sendResponse: sanitizes the callback once, so content-type selection, streaming, and non-streaming paths all use the safe value.\n- JolokiaHttpHandler.sendStreamingResponse and sendAllJSON: sanitize the callback read from ParsedUri.\n- IoUtil.streamResponseAndClose: re-validates its callback argument as defense-in-depth (drops invalid callbacks and streams plain JSON).\n\nInvalid/malicious callbacks are silently dropped rather than throwing, because the callback is consumed inside the `finally`/sendResponse phase (even error responses are wrapped in the callback); returning plain JSON there keeps the response well-formed while guaranteeing no reflection. Legitimate JSONP with normal function names is unaffected.\n\nAdded IoUtilTest cases covering accepted names, rejected XSS payloads, and end-to-end proof that a `<script>` callback is not reflected in the streamed output.",
        "regression_commands": [
          "mvn -B -pl agent/core -am test -Dtest=IoUtilTest -DfailIfNoTests=false"
        ],
        "risk_notes": "Behavior change: a `callback` value that is not a valid JavaScript function name is now ignored and the endpoint returns plain JSON instead of a JSONP wrapper. Legitimate clients using normal function-name callbacks (including dotted namespaces) are unaffected. Note: pre-existing test failures exist in agent/jvm's JolokiaHttpHandlerTest (12/17) caused by an environment/JDK issue in the test's prepareExchange setup (NullPointerException in com.sun.net.httpserver.Headers.set) — these fail identically on the unmodified baseline and are unrelated to this patch. The recommended regression command targets IoUtilTest in agent/core, which passes.",
        "status": "patched",
